WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:08.059 --> 00:00:13.070
Unless you live in a cave and your only source
of information is VisualPolitik, in which

00:00:13.070 --> 00:00:14.599
case, Thank you!

00:00:14.599 --> 00:00:18.020
You probably know that Fidel Castro has died.

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:21.260
And with his death, a communist icon goes
away.

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:26.119
He ruled over Cuba with an iron fist, for
more than 50 years.

00:00:26.119 --> 00:00:30.630
Now many people wonder whether Fidel´s death
will be the first step in a transition for

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:31.630
Cuba.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:35.620
A transition from a communist dictatorship
to a liberal democracy.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:41.930
But the reality is that Fidel retired from
poltics in 2008, handing power over to his

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:44.180
little brother, Raul Castro.

00:00:44.180 --> 00:00:46.730
Keeping Cuba in the family business.

00:00:46.730 --> 00:00:51.370
The truth is Raul had found himself forced
to apply several reforms.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:55.210
Reforms that, not so long time ago, would
have been impossible to imagine in a regime

00:00:55.210 --> 00:00:59.629
that touted itself as the paragon of a traditional
communist system.

00:00:59.629 --> 00:01:04.239
Clearly, Castro-ism is done, at least the
way we know it.

00:01:04.239 --> 00:01:06.450
No one knows what will it become of Cuba.

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:10.360
But one thing it for sure: it´s changing.

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:14.420
Well you all asked for a video about Cuba,
and, as you know, here in VisualPolitik, we

00:01:14.420 --> 00:01:16.109
like to think outside the box.

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:20.460
So were answering what we think is a very
important question that hasn’t yet been

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:21.460
answered:

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:23.970
Is now a good moment to invest in Cuba?

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:29.610
Can you make money out of the political changes
expected on the island?

00:01:29.610 --> 00:01:34.509
Today we will answer that question.

00:01:34.509 --> 00:01:39.351
History shows that when a country goes from
a planned economy to a free market one, there

00:01:39.351 --> 00:01:43.179
is a window of opportunity where you can make
a fortune.

00:01:43.179 --> 00:01:48.649
A good example is the building I’m in right
now.

00:01:48.649 --> 00:01:50.189
I British, but I live in Prague in the Czech
Republic.

00:01:50.189 --> 00:01:55.719
Now at the beginning of the 1990s the Czech
Republic was opening their economy after decades

00:01:55.719 --> 00:01:56.789
of communism.

00:01:56.789 --> 00:02:03.200
This means that, for the first time in years,
you could buy and sell houses.

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.350
But not only that!

00:02:06.350 --> 00:02:10.270
Since the country was relatively poor, prices
where insanely cheap.

00:02:10.270 --> 00:02:14.630
This attracted a lot of foreign investors,
specifically from the north of Italy, they

00:02:14.630 --> 00:02:18.010
bought properties for almost no money.

00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:22.260
Years later, the Czech economy started growing
fast.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:26.950
Foreign companies settled down here, tourists
came, locals created companies, etc…

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:35.550
So, in a short time, houses doubled their
prices and made owners into millionaires.

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:38.750
A very similar thing might happen in Cuba.

00:02:38.750 --> 00:02:40.379
But hold on a second!

00:02:40.379 --> 00:02:42.330
This is not quite as simple as it sounds.

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:46.700
Other former communist countries like Ukraine
didn’t have the same luck and more than

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:51.269
one investor in that country has gone bankrupt
because of poor investments.

00:02:51.269 --> 00:02:54.810
Before considering investing in Cuba, it’s
important to understand what´s going on in

00:02:54.810 --> 00:02:57.980
the country and the reforms they are implementing.

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:01.760
But, before we get into that, let´s take
a look at the countries history.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:04.790
TITLE: THE SITUATION IN CUBA, TODAY

00:03:04.790 --> 00:03:06.620
Cuba is a communist country.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:10.750
This means their whole economy is directed
by the government.

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:15.909
For some clarity, in the “good times”,
the Cuban government employed 92% of the nations

00:03:15.909 --> 00:03:16.909
workforce.

00:03:16.909 --> 00:03:19.960
This means almost everyone was working in
the public sector.

00:03:19.960 --> 00:03:25.220
Those where the 80s, when Cuba exported sugar,
tobacco, and all kinds of fruits to Soviet

00:03:25.220 --> 00:03:26.220
Union.

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:31.159
But in 1989 the Berlin Wall fell and Fidel
Castro lost his main trade partner.

00:03:31.159 --> 00:03:36.840
Add to this the US embargo, which forbids
American companies to do any kind of business

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:41.200
with the island, and Cuba was practically
isolated from the rest of the world.

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:46.440
This resulted in a brutal economic crisis
that lasted until the year 2000, when Hugo

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:48.700
Chavez came to power in Venezuela.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:53.150
As we will see in another video, Venezuela
used to be an oil-rich country, and since

00:03:53.150 --> 00:03:59.390
Chavez and Castro were such good buddies,
Cuba got plenty of this oil-money from Caracas

00:03:59.390 --> 00:04:00.390
government.

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:01.620
This was a life raft for Castro´s revolución.

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:08.730
Nevertheless, in the year 2013, oil prices
collapsed and so did Venezuela’s economy.

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:12.980
And, of course, Cuba followed suit.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:17.390
Now, at this time, Fidel was already retired
and his brother, Raúl, had taken the reins

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:18.390
of the country.

00:04:18.390 --> 00:04:23.110
Raúl Castro realized that Cuba was once again
isolated, and he needed to change a lot of

00:04:23.110 --> 00:04:29.229
things… otherwise his country was going
to get a lot worse.

00:04:29.229 --> 00:04:32.930
TITLE: RAUL CASTRO´S CHINESE REFORMS

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:40.330
By the way, the music in todays video is from
Rik, a singer, composer and guitar player

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:41.740
from Medellin, Colombia.

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:53.479
If you like him, you will find his channel
on the links I put on you on the description.

00:04:53.479 --> 00:05:00.059
Okay, back to 2013, and Raul Castro is announcing
a package of small, but meaningful reforms.

00:05:00.059 --> 00:05:02.150
The first one, was the legalization of the
so called, “CUENTAPROPISTAS”, something

00:05:02.150 --> 00:05:06.310
similar to what we would call “freelancers.”

00:05:06.310 --> 00:05:09.509
For the first time, Cubans could start small
businesses.

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:12.530
Now there were still a lot of restrictions.

00:05:12.530 --> 00:05:16.490
For example, they couldn’t hire anyone and
they could only start a business in one of

00:05:16.490 --> 00:05:17.810
the industries permitted by the government.

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:25.660
However, in the 3 years since, this “CUENTAPROPISTAS”
have grown to represent 10% of the Cuban workforce.

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:31.840
“Before people weren’t doing anything
private because government would take it away

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:38.240
from them… but now, the government trusts
the cuentapropistas because they are the future”.

00:05:38.240 --> 00:05:40.160
But hold on just a moment because there is
more!

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:45.319
In fact, Raul Castro seems to be following
Chinese Communist Party´s playbook (which,

00:05:45.319 --> 00:05:48.830
by the way, will be the topic of another video
we’re launching soon.)

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:55.820
Actually, in a very DEN XIAOPING style, Raul
has created his own “Special Economic Zone”,

00:05:55.820 --> 00:05:59.229
the so called “MARIEL Development Zone”.

00:05:59.229 --> 00:06:00.229
What does this mean?

00:06:00.229 --> 00:06:04.660
Well… inside of this zone, foreign companies
are allowed to start businesses, as well as

00:06:04.660 --> 00:06:09.570
hire local people, and trade with less restrictions
than in the rest of Cuba

00:06:09.570 --> 00:06:18.400
“Five foreign companies, two Cuban and a
multi-country one, are the first eight companies

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:23.879
in the Mariel Development Zone, which is to
become the main economic center of Cuba”

00:06:23.879 --> 00:06:28.470
Now you might be wondering: How is that possible
that an international company, like the Spanish

00:06:28.470 --> 00:06:33.370
based Barcelo Hotels is already in Cuba if,
apparently, there is a ban for foreign companies

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:34.370
to set up there?

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:38.210
If you’re watching this video from somewhere
outside of US, you might have travelled to

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:39.590
Havana in some point in your life.

00:06:39.590 --> 00:06:44.160
If that´s the case, you probably were staying
in a Barcelo or a Melia hotel.

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:48.650
These are Spanish companies and they have
been operating in the Cuban market since the

00:06:48.650 --> 00:06:52.490
year 2000.

00:06:52.490 --> 00:06:57.289
But the truth is, in order to establish themselves
on the island, both firms needed to partner

00:06:57.289 --> 00:06:58.990
with Castro´s government.

00:06:58.990 --> 00:07:04.690
This means, the hotels are owned by the government
and the companies have a licence to manage

00:07:04.690 --> 00:07:06.680
them and get a share of the profit.

00:07:06.680 --> 00:07:10.070
So, until now, it was impossible to start
any kind of business in Cuba.

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:12.500
Unless you made a partnership with the authorities.

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:15.879
So the creation of the Special Economic Zone
shows a clear trend.

00:07:15.879 --> 00:07:18.810
A trend that we also saw in China in the 90s.

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:22.039
Further to this, there is the freeing up of
the housing market.

00:07:22.039 --> 00:07:26.009
In just two years, over 40,000 houses have
been sold in Cuba.

00:07:26.009 --> 00:07:29.610
Now this doesn’t exactly mean that Cubans
have private property and, the transactions

00:07:29.610 --> 00:07:33.300
come with a thousand different restrictions,
but it does highlight the fact that there

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:37.050
is a trend occurring in the country.

00:07:37.050 --> 00:07:42.909
The most important news in recent times of
course, was Obama´s announcement that the

00:07:42.909 --> 00:07:46.470
trade embargo with Cuba was coming to an end.

00:07:46.470 --> 00:07:47.470
The problem?

00:07:47.470 --> 00:07:50.280
It still needs to be passed by the American
congress.

00:07:50.280 --> 00:08:15.789
And, with Donald Trump as the new president,
it is hard to predict what´s going to happen

00:08:15.789 --> 00:08:19.250
next.

00:08:19.250 --> 00:08:23.740
If Trump were to keep the trade block with
Cuba, this would be bad news for many investors

00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:25.060
in the United States.

00:08:25.060 --> 00:08:28.490
They would lose out on business opportunities
in Cuba to investors from other nations without

00:08:28.490 --> 00:08:34.720
such trade restrictions, for example, British,
Canadian or Australian investors.

00:08:34.720 --> 00:08:35.720
&nbsp;

00:08:35.720 --> 00:08:36.720
But hold on a moment!

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:40.140
There is no guarantee that Cuba will become
a free market paradise overnight.

00:08:40.140 --> 00:08:46.410
It´s not even clear that investing in the
country right now is a good idea.

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:49.760
In fact, there are two potential scenarios
that could play our here.

00:08:49.760 --> 00:08:53.961
One would be that Cuba follows the example
of Czechoslovakia (now two nations, the Czech

00:08:53.961 --> 00:08:59.230
Republic and Slovakia), or they follow example
of the Ukraine.

00:08:59.230 --> 00:09:03.910
Now let’s have a look at these two very
different examples:

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:08.360
TITLE: CZECHOSLOVAKIA VERSUS UKRAINE

00:09:08.360 --> 00:09:12.800
In 1990, both Czecoslovakia and Ukraine abandoned
a communism based system.

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:15.390
But there is a big difference here.

00:09:15.390 --> 00:09:19.520
The Czechs had a revolution, named the “velvet
revolution”, in order to overthrow their

00:09:19.520 --> 00:09:20.520
dictator.

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:24.160
And the new government, led by this guy you
see on the screen, whose name is VACLAV HAVEL,

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:26.610
sent home the old guard who were ruling the
country.

00:09:26.610 --> 00:09:30.750
Meanwhile over in Ukraine, despite the fact
they had gotten their independence from Soviet

00:09:30.750 --> 00:09:33.640
Union they kept the same political elite…

00:09:33.640 --> 00:09:38.980
Their new president, LEONID KRAVCHUK, came
from the Old Soviet Communist Party.

00:09:38.980 --> 00:09:40.880
But this is not the end of the story!

00:09:40.880 --> 00:09:45.120
Just like Cuba, Ukraine and Czechoslovakia
had planned economies where all the companies

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:46.640
belonged to the government.

00:09:46.640 --> 00:09:51.460
The first step in opening up their economies
was privatization.

00:09:51.460 --> 00:09:58.200
But importantly, not all privatizations are
equal!

00:09:58.200 --> 00:10:02.240
The Czechs took their biggest companies and
made a calculation of their economic value.

00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:06.680
Then, they divided the economic value of these
companies into “vouchers”.

00:10:06.680 --> 00:10:10.500
If you were a Czech citizen, you had the right
to buy one of these vouchers by a reasonable

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:13.870
price - something equal to a week of the average
salary.

00:10:13.870 --> 00:10:18.079
This is why 80% of the eligible population
bought a voucher.

00:10:18.079 --> 00:10:22.800
With this paper in your hand, you had the
right to bid for some shares in the company.

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:26.829
In order to help those who didn’t know how
to bid for shares the Czech government encouraged

00:10:26.829 --> 00:10:28.430
the creation of hedge funds.

00:10:28.430 --> 00:10:32.459
Those hedge funds advised common citizens
on how to invest intelligently.

00:10:32.459 --> 00:10:36.980
A Czech citizen could go to one of these hedge
funds and ask: “I want to get some shares

00:10:36.980 --> 00:10:41.030
of this company, and that one, etc”.

00:10:41.030 --> 00:10:46.170
Now, as you can probably imagine, there was
a lot of corruption here…

00:10:46.170 --> 00:10:48.380
But it also had a really positive outcome.

00:10:48.380 --> 00:10:54.260
It helped the majority of the Czechs to benefit
from the privatization of the nations companies.

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:55.660
And the proof is in the pudding.

00:10:55.660 --> 00:11:01.200
Today, 25 years later, the Czech Republic
is as egalitarian as Germany and has a quality

00:11:01.200 --> 00:11:06.640
of life as good as anywhere else in Europe.

00:11:06.640 --> 00:11:12.860
But, the story in Ukraine is very very different.

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:17.649
Now Ukraine did also sell these vouchers to
their citizens: If you were a Ukrainian citizen,

00:11:17.649 --> 00:11:22.610
you could buy a voucher and, eventually, bid
for some shares.

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:26.590
But the reality is the government never got
around to arranging those biddings.

00:11:26.590 --> 00:11:31.180
It only happened in the case of the smallest
and worse companies.

00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:35.850
Ukrainians were left waiting for years, with
their vouchers in hand, waiting for the moment

00:11:35.850 --> 00:11:37.350
to exchange them for something valuable.

00:11:37.350 --> 00:11:41.950
And during this time, Ukraine was also suffering
from an all-time-high inflation rate.

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:46.269
When purchased, the vouchers were worth about
1,500 USD…

00:11:46.269 --> 00:11:51.690
Some years later, they were being exchanged
on the black market for as little as 10 USD.

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:57.170
So the average Ukrainian would be sitting
at home, and an oligarch would come knocking.

00:11:57.170 --> 00:12:00.760
And he’d say something like “Woah, what
you going to do with that voucher?

00:12:00.760 --> 00:12:02.460
It’s never going to be worth anything to
you.

00:12:02.460 --> 00:12:07.240
Tell you what: You give it to me, and I’ll
give you some money that you can actually

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:08.240
use!”

00:12:08.240 --> 00:12:12.420
And surprise surprise soon enough all the
vouchers were on the hands of these oligarchs

00:12:12.420 --> 00:12:18.170
(and, no prizes for guessing this one, but
those oligarchs were pretty closely tied to

00:12:18.170 --> 00:12:20.579
the government, who then decided it was time
to auction off some of those companies)!

00:12:20.579 --> 00:12:26.230
The outcome?

00:12:26.230 --> 00:12:29.760
Only those companies which were interesting
for the oligarchs where sold.

00:12:29.760 --> 00:12:33.980
This is why Ukraine is still to make some
privatizations today.

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:42.110
But the most important thing is that 85% of
Ukraine´s wealth is now in the hands of its

00:12:42.110 --> 00:12:43.519
50 wealthiest oligarchs.

00:12:43.519 --> 00:12:48.430
This results in no political stability and
a horrific climate for investment.

00:12:48.430 --> 00:12:52.010
(Oh, and not to mention that war with Russia).

00:12:52.010 --> 00:12:56.760
So if an investor had bought property in Kiev
10 years ago, they might be hitting their

00:12:56.760 --> 00:12:59.589
head against a wall right about now…

00:12:59.589 --> 00:13:02.990
Alright, let´s go back to Cuba!

00:13:02.990 --> 00:13:05.990
Here we have some things that resemble Ukraine
and others that reminds us of Czechoslovakia.

00:13:05.990 --> 00:13:07.380
On the one hand, Cuba has a family, the Castro
family, who controls everything and won´t

00:13:07.380 --> 00:13:08.380
leave power easily.

00:13:08.380 --> 00:13:09.380
Plus, there are no charismatic alternatives
(someone like Vaclav Havel in Czechoslovakia,

00:13:09.380 --> 00:13:10.380
who had enough support from the people to
overthrow a dictator without violence.)

00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:11.380
On the other hand, Cuba has a big and influential
geographically scattered population.

00:13:11.380 --> 00:13:12.880
For example, in US you have more than 2 million
Cubans living, which represents 20% of the

00:13:12.880 --> 00:13:15.050
entire Cuban population.

00:13:15.050 --> 00:13:19.372
These Cuban Americans have been educated in
a democratic system and could help to build

00:13:19.372 --> 00:13:22.070
good democratic institutions in Cuba.

00:13:22.070 --> 00:13:28.440
If this was the case, Cuba might become a
place with the rule of law, civil rights,

00:13:28.440 --> 00:13:32.990
and many opportunities to help Cubans make
money and lift themselves out of poverty.

00:13:32.990 --> 00:13:40.190
This is our opinion, now we want to hear yours.

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:41.410
What do you think it is going to happen in
Cuba?

00:13:41.410 --> 00:13:45.060
Will they follow the path of the Czech Republic
or the path of Ukraine?

00:13:45.060 --> 00:13:47.610
Please, let us know in the comments below.

